  "description": "`target.hostkey_refused`: the operator refused a first-use host key in a device login. The core writes it before it relays the refusal to the worker, so the line records the operator's decision (L3); a refusal whose line cannot be written is logged and the refusal goes on, since a refusal records nothing. `user` is the TSB principal who refused, `detail` the fingerprint and the connection. No session exists, so no session_id. The matching acceptance is `target.hostkey_accepted`, which on a prompt-mode connect records the operator's decision, whether or not the worker then records the key.",
  "corpus": [
    "decision 5.18",
    "Storage §6",
    "device-login step 13",
    "open_decisions §5"
  ],
  "case": {
